<!-- 11. PRODUCT METRICS -->
<section class="section slide-page" id="product-metrics">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">09 · Product Metrics</span><h2>Prioritisation frameworks and product metrics used in regulated digital banking</h2></div>
      <p>These tools reflect realistic product-management practice for fintech and digital banking platforms, where decisions must balance customer value, regulatory criticality, implementation constraints and operational risk.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="metrics-grid reveal">
      <div class="metrics-panel">
        <h3>Prioritisation frameworks</h3>
        <div class="framework-list">
          <div class="framework-card" style="--tone:#2f6fe5;">
            <h4>RICE</h4>
            <p>Prioritise regulated features by reach, impact, confidence and effort, particularly when deciding between onboarding improvements, AML controls, reconciliation workflows, or API enhancements across multiple bank implementations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="framework-card" style="--tone:#5c6be3;">
            <h4>MoSCoW</h4>
            <p>Separate must-have compliance and customer-critical workflows from should-have improvements so releases remain aligned to legal obligations, service continuity and migration readiness.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="framework-card" style="--tone:#1a9c7c;">
            <h4>Impact vs. Effort</h4>
            <p>Use this to sequence reusable platform capabilities such as workflow configuration, document upload, exception handling, and reporting dashboards across the product suite.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="framework-card" style="--tone:#d08d1d;">
            <h4>WSJF</h4>
            <p>Apply weighted short-job-first thinking where business urgency, regulatory dependency and customer friction are combined into a single prioritisation view for roadmap decisions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="metrics-panel">
        <h3>Product metrics</h3>
        <div class="metric-list">
          <div class="metric-pair">
            <div class="metric-group">
              <div class="metric-card" style="--tone:#2f6fe5;">
                <h4>Adoption Rate</h4>
                <p>Track percent of bank users or teams actively using a workflow after deployment.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="metric-card" style="--tone:#1a9c7c;">
                <h4>Transaction Success Rate</h4>
                <p>Measure successful completion of payments, lending actions, reconciliations, and operational flows.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="metric-card" style="--tone:#d08d1d;">
                <h4>Exception Rate</h4>
                <p>Identify failed or manually worked cases requiring intervention across integrations and operational functions.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="metric-group">
              <div class="metric-card" style="--tone:#7b5de7;">
                <h4>STP Rate</h4>
                <p>Monitor straight-through processing for credit, payment, and compliance case handling.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="metric-card" style="--tone:#ba4d8c;">
                <h4>API Success Rate</h4>
                <p>Track the success of external calls to CBS, payment rails, credit bureaus and compliance services.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="metric-card" style="--tone:#3198a0;">
                <h4>Reconciliation Accuracy</h4>
                <p>Measure the percent of transaction records matching without manual adjustment or defect escalation.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="relationship">
          <b>Product → Use case → Metric → Impact</b>
          <p><strong>Loan origination:</strong> Application completion rate and turnaround time → reduced processing delays and better credit operations.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="metrics-panel" style="grid-column:1 / -1;">
        <h3>Portfolio-relevant decision lens</h3>
        <div class="metric-list">
          <div class="metric-card" style="--tone:#6f96e8;"><h4>Risk Reduction</h4><p>Prioritise controls, alerting, validation and exception handling where compliance exposure and operational risk are highest.</p></div>
          <div class="metric-card" style="--tone:#5ca580;"><h4>Customer / Business Impact</h4><p>Weight improvements by effect on user experience, clearances, turnaround time and operational efficiency for banks, NBFCs and support teams.</p></div>
          <div class="metric-card" style="--tone:#b77a2f;"><h4>Dependency-based prioritisation</h4><p>Sequence work according to external dependencies, data migration readiness, integration contracts and downstream approvals that can block delivery.</p></div>
          <div class="metric-card" style="--tone:#ba5d8d;"><h4>Regulatory / Criticality-based prioritisation</h4><p>Promote compliance, AML, KYC, audit and control functionalities ahead of low-risk enhancements when criticality and legal obligations justify it.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

